//api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810383507","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105387#issuecomment-2810383507","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105387","id":2810383507,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ngwyT","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T18:26:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T18:26:10Z","body":"As @AThousandShips said, we use the same issue to track lack of support for other collections (not just list).\n\nTo be more clear, `bool[]` is specifically not supported because there's no `PackedBoolArray` in Godot. The only C# arrays supported are the ones with a matching packed array type.\n\nAs mentioned in the linked issue, you can use `Godot.Collections.Array<bool>` instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810383507/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]